{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent low-bias: forecasts are systematically below realized prices, especially from ~day 10 onward when the market trends up. Apply an upward level shift (increasing with horizon).",
    "Trend/acceleration underreaction: when history transitions from a dip to a rebound, the model follows but with insufficient slope; it misses sustained rallies. Add a momentum/trend term that increases forecasts when the last 5–10 days show positive drift.",
    "Horizon-dependent error: near-term (days 1–5) errors are small/mixed, but medium-to-long horizon (days ~10–30) errors become strongly negative. Use a correction that ramps up with forecast step (e.g., linear or convex uplift by lead time).",
    "Lag after regime change: the model behaves as if mean-reverting to the recent range, while outcomes break to a higher regime (mid/high 60s). Detect breakouts (price > recent 10–20d band) and reduce mean-reversion strength / shift the anchor upward.",
    "Amplitude compression: forecast volatility is too low versus outcomes during rallies (peaks capped ~66–67 while realized reaches ~69–70). Increase forecast variance/upper tail when trend is positive and recent realized volatility is rising."
  ]
}
